{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02795",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.59,
      "end_seconds": 4.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "Uh, hello, doctor. May I come in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.22,
      "end_seconds": 11.43,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "No problem at all, come in. What's troubling you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.6,
      "end_seconds": 18.4,
      "duration_seconds": 5.8,
      "text": "So the thing is, I've got difficulty getting out of bed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 20.21,
      "end_seconds": 34.87,
      "duration_seconds": 14.66,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. BP is 120 over 70, SpO2 99 percent on room air. BMI works out to 29.2, height 158 centimetres, weight 73 kilos, heart rate 86, temp 36.5 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 36.08,
      "end_seconds": 37.63,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 54.82,
      "end_seconds": 56.81,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "Did it come on recently?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 58.19,
      "end_seconds": 61.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "I've had it since last Tuesday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 65.24,
      "end_seconds": 69.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "Is it a lot or only a little?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 70.57,
      "end_seconds": 73.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "Pretty severe, if I'm being honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.48,
      "end_seconds": 77.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "Have you had a mild temperature?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.67,
      "end_seconds": 95.22,
      "duration_seconds": 13.55,
      "text": "Yeah. About a month, I'd say. And there's stiff aching shoulders and hips as well, six months now. With stiff aching shoulders and hips, moderate, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.8,
      "end_seconds": 102.92,
      "duration_seconds": 7.12,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any headache, jaw pain on chewing, weight loss or visual changes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.27,
      "end_seconds": 107.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "No, I'd have said so."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.15,
      "end_seconds": 113.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "Anything with your heart, like skipped beats or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 115.01,
      "end_seconds": 117.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "No, nothing with my heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 118.87,
      "end_seconds": 124.2,
      "duration_seconds": 5.33,
      "text": "Has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 125.17,
      "end_seconds": 135.78,
      "duration_seconds": 10.61,
      "text": "I, I had a reaction to amoxicillin when I was younger, a rash all over, and I've avoided it since."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.24,
      "end_seconds": 140.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "Are you in work at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.08,
      "end_seconds": 145.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "Yes, I work in a bakery, early starts."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.96,
      "end_seconds": 150.16,
      "duration_seconds": 1.2,
      "text": "Are you active?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.24,
      "end_seconds": 154.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "I walk the dog every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.48,
      "end_seconds": 158.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "Okay, is there someone at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.35,
      "end_seconds": 163.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.45,
      "text": "My husband and I live above the shop."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 168.26,
      "end_seconds": 170.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "Tell me your medicines, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.72,
      "end_seconds": 175.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "Bisoprolol. I take it once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.09,
      "end_seconds": 179.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "How much do you take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.48,
      "end_seconds": 185.53,
      "duration_seconds": 5.05,
      "text": "2.5 milligrams, I think that's what's on the box."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.99,
      "end_seconds": 193.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "Anything in your past medical history I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 195.36,
      "end_seconds": 199.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "I've had an irregular heartbeat for five years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.29,
      "end_seconds": 207.35,
      "duration_seconds": 6.06,
      "text": "Understood. Yes, an irregular heartbeat is known to us, good to have that clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.44,
      "end_seconds": 213.88,
      "duration_seconds": 4.44,
      "text": "I'd like to check you over now, if that's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 230.0,
      "end_seconds": 230.96,
      "duration_seconds": 0.96,
      "text": "Sure thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 231.94,
      "end_seconds": 233.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "Hold that for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.77,
      "end_seconds": 258.43,
      "duration_seconds": 6.66,
      "text": "The shoulders are painful to move but strength is normal and there is no joint swelling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 260.14,
      "end_seconds": 261.17,
      "duration_seconds": 1.03,
      "text": "Sure thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.17,
      "end_seconds": 265.98,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "Please sit back down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.59,
      "end_seconds": 282.74,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "Having listened and examined, it points towards polymyalgia rheumatica."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 284.22,
      "end_seconds": 287.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "Is there something to worry about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.63,
      "end_seconds": 298.65,
      "duration_seconds": 10.02,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with polymyalgia rheumatica do well once it's treated properly. I'll request blood tests, it'll help with proximal stiffness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 299.57,
      "end_seconds": 301.19,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "Does it hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.39,
      "end_seconds": 323.23,
      "duration_seconds": 20.84,
      "text": "For this, prednisolone, 15 milligrams, once a day, reducing course. You take it by mouth. It's for polymyalgia rheumatica. The pharmacy will go through the details again when you pick it up. Report any headache or jaw pain immediately. What are the next steps as you understand them?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 325.31,
      "end_seconds": 333.85,
      "duration_seconds": 8.54,
      "text": "So, um, I take the prednisolone, 15 milligrams, once a day. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 335.15,
      "end_seconds": 340.4,
      "duration_seconds": 5.25,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 341.57,
      "end_seconds": 343.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Thank you, doctor, goodbye."
    }
  ]
}